  "comments": "There are 2 variants for this coin (Krause):<br /><br />\r\nKM# 120.1 Minted at Buenos Aires, dated 2003, has no mintmark, and also the neck of the bust points between &quot;P&quot; and &quot;U&quot; on &quot;REPÚBLICA&quot;.<br /><br />\r\nKM# 120.2 Minted at Santiago dated 2005 and 2008 has the mintmark under bust; the neck of the bust points directly to the &quot;P&quot; on &quot;REPÚBLICA&quot;.<br /><br />\r\n2005 version is softer than 2003 and 2008 (stronger relief of details).<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/60e10136a3b36.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/60e10136a3b36.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\nKM# 120.1 on right, KM# 120.2 on left<br />\r\n© adanieluy<br /><br />\r\nVariants:<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2003:</span><br />\r\nSA# 143.1.1, CG# 168.1.A, coin rotation,<br />\r\nSA# 143.1.2, CG# 168.1.B, medal rotation (normal issue),<br />\r\nSA# 143.1.3, CG# 168.1.C, 90º or 270º rotation,<br />\r\nSA# 143.1.4, CG# 168.1.D, other rotation.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2005:</span><br />\r\nSA# 147.1.2, CG# 176.1.B, medal rotation (normal issue),<br />\r\nSA# 147.1.4, CG# 176.1.D, other rotation.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2008:</span><br />\r\nNo variations",
